    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "742aaacb0b7160b0793e962d6368981d4b971033e90a13659436387435d7bdd6",
      "text": "After breakfast at the hotel, transfer to the airport for your flight to Cusco. You'll be met on arrival and taken to your hotel.\n\nIn the afternoon, you’ll tour the archaeological sites around Cusco, beginning with Sacsayhuamán, which dates to Inca times. According to legend, people from other tribes were barred from the sacred complex, and only a ruler of royal blood could govern it.\n\nNext, visit Qorikancha, the Temple of the Sun. Tradition holds that in the 15th century its walls and interior were decorated with gold and its altar took the form of a golden disc. After the Spanish arrived, the temple was destroyed and a monastery was built on the site. An earthquake later damaged the Spanish building, revealing the massive slabs of the original Inca stonework.\n\nContinue to Tambomachay, a site associated with water and ritual bathing. Specially built channels carried water into the pools here. Nearby stands Puka Pukara, the “Red Fort”, which served as a guard post. Return to your hotel for an overnight stay in Cusco.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-1ec1641096b2",
        "model": "GPT-6 Codex"
      }
